          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What has come to be called
            %em nonabelian T-duality
            (
            %a{:href => "#OssaQuevedo92"}> de la Ossa-Quevedo 1992
            ) or
            %em Poisson-Lie T-Duality
            (due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#KlimcikSevera95"} Klimcik-Ševera 1995
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#vonUnge02"} von Unge 02
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles"} fiber bundles
            equipped with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometries"} isometries
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundles"} bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+group"} nonabelian group
            of isometries.
          %p
            Poisson-Lie T-duality may also be made manifest at the level of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity"} type II supergravity
            in the framework of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+field+theory"} double field theory
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} group manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR+fields"} RR fields
            for full Poisson-Lie T-duality (
            %a{:href => "#Hassler17"}> Hassler 17
            ).
          %h2#as_a_partial_duality_of_string_theory As a partial duality of string theory
          %p
            While ordinary abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            is supposedly a full
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality in string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+perturbation+series"} string perturbation series
            to all orders of the squared
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+length"} string length
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Regge+slope"} Regge slope
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha'
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+coupling+constant"} string coupling constant
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_s
            %a{:href => "#Rocek93"} Giveon &amp; Roček 1993
            that there are topological
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstructions"} obstructions
            at higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus+of+a+surface"} genus
            for non-abelian T-duality, letting it break down in higher orders of
            = succeed ";" do
